 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- Add a `dotenv check` command that lists keys present in an example file (`--example`, default `.env.example` next to the `.env` file) but missing from the `.env` file, exiting with code 1 if any are missing
+- Add a `dotenv diff A B` command that lists keys only in A, keys only in B and keys whose values differ (key names only, never values), exiting with code 1 if the files differ
+
 ### Fixed
 
 - Fix a package build deprecation warning caused by a non-string `license` value in `pyproject.toml` by [@kurtmckee] in [#648]
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 3400e67..87cfbe5 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -162,9 +162,19 @@ $ dotenv list --format=json
   "USER": "foo",
   "EMAIL": "foo@example.org"
 }
+$ dotenv check --example .env.example
+API_KEY
 $ dotenv run -- python foo.py
 ```
 
+`dotenv check` lists the keys defined in the example file (`.env.example` next
+to the `.env` file by default) that are missing from `.env`, and exits with
+code 1 if there are any.
+
+`dotenv diff A B` compares two env files and prints `< KEY` for keys only in A,
+`> KEY` for keys only in B and `~ KEY` for keys whose values differ. Only key
+names are printed, never values. It exits with code 1 if the files differ.
+
 Run `dotenv --help` for more information about the options and subcommands.
 
 ## File format
